Code baseline
-------------
Quilla's code baseline is derived from Contiki-NG
(https://github.com/contiki-ng/contiki-ng), which is distributed under the
3-clause BSD license. Files inherited from Contiki-NG keep their original
copyright headers in place, including notices such as
"Copyright (c) 2004-2006, Swedish Institute of Computer Science" and the
other upstream notices present in those files.

The original upstream README is preserved as CONTIKI-README.md. Upstream
documentation under doc/upstream/ is kept verbatim; it describes Contiki-NG,
not Quilla (see doc/upstream/README.md).

Quilla-owned code
-----------------
The dual-partition QBOOT bootloader, the QIAP upgrade protocol, secure boot,
host tools and Quilla's own documentation are
Copyright (c) 2026 JiChiRen Info. Tech. and are distributed under the
3-clause BSD license (see LICENSE.md). Derived files additionally carry
this copyright line alongside the retained upstream notice.

Attribution boundaries
----------------------
Quilla is an independent derivative of Contiki-NG. It is not endorsed by,
sponsored by, or affiliated with the Contiki-NG project or its maintainers.
The Contiki-NG name is used solely to state the factual origin of the code.

Third-party material
--------------------
Vendor HAL / CMSIS files under arch/cpu/ keep their original copyright and
license headers. Each file's own header is authoritative for its terms.
The demo keypair under tools/_keytest/ is intentionally public and is for
development only; it is not a security control.

